From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:45:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor: the review of Tier 87 fixed (scratch per
 compositor, GL objects freed per card, late reads)

T-513, the review of the GPU path (two inspectors; context/impl/impl-review-findings-gpu-2.md, E1-E7):

- E1: the band scratch's size is the compositor's own (mJihadBandScratchSize), not a function-static
  shared by all: with two cards one was handed a buffer another had outgrown and glReadPixels wrote
  past it.
- E2: a closed card's frame-sized and band pbuffers are destroyed with its context, and
  CompositorOGL::CleanupResources deletes the window targets', the band target's and the swizzle
  pass's renderbuffers, framebuffers, texture and program: in the process-long share group each closed
  card left ~13-16 MB of GPU memory. Twenty open/close cycles now add 76 KB.
- E3: a band frame of 257-320 rows stacked in the frame-sized target makes that surface current first
  (on the Adreno 220 every target must match the current surface).
- E4: a WebGL canvas's texture source is externally owned (the producer's SharedSurface deletes the
  name; in one share group the second delete could hit a name handed out again).
- E5: the reads carry their request's cancel flag (JihadSetCancel): a read given up past the daemon's
  bound stops after glReadPixels, before the swizzle and any copy into the slot; a whole read (straight
  into the slot) is counted, jihad_offscreen_late_writes(), and the daemon then paints every slot whole.
- E6: a frame whose chunks would pass the 12-band cap of one composite takes the whole path instead
  of reading chunks it did not compose.
- E7: a sticky layer's stuck probe reaches twice the composite's scroll step (64 to 1024 px), so a fast
  flick's step no longer slides its old pixels with the content.

Codex on the fixes (2026-10-24, C1): the opt-in read paths stop for a given-up frame as well: the
scratch read before its copy into the slot, the swizzle pass and the read thread after their read
(counted as late writes), the read thread also before it, and a cancelled read-thread frame is not
reported good.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
